#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At al-‘Aqabah one pilgrimage season, the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ recited the Quran to six men from Yathrib, who lived beside Jews. “By Allah,” they said to one another, “this is the prophet the Jews threatened you with.”"
msgstr "Katika al-‘Aqabah, wakati wa msimu mmoja wa hija, Mtume Muhammad ﷺ aliwasomea Qurani wanaume sita kutoka Yathrib, waliokuwa wakiishi karibu na Wayahudi. “Wallahi,” wakaambiana, “huyu ndiye nabii ambaye Wayahudi waliwaonya kuhusu yeye.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One pilgrimage season, six men from the town of Yathrib listened to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, and believed."
msgstr "Wakati wa msimu mmoja wa hija, wanaume sita kutoka mji wa Yathrib walimsikiliza Mtume Muhammad ﷺ na wakaamini."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each year more came, until seventy-three men and two women met him there by night and pledged to protect him as they protected their own women and children. “I am of you and you are of me,” he said."
msgstr "Kila mwaka watu zaidi walikuja, mpaka wanaume sabini na watatu na wanawake wawili walipokutana naye huko usiku na kuahidi kumlinda kama walivyolinda wanawake na watoto wao wenyewe. “Mimi ni wenu, nanyi ni wangu,” akasema."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Later, many more came at night. They promised to keep him safe, just like their own families."
msgstr "Baadaye, watu wengi zaidi walikuja usiku. Waliahidi kumlinda kama walivyolinda familia zao wenyewe."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "“It is Yathrib,” he told his companions, and group after group they slipped away to Madinah. At last, of those free to go, only he, Abu Bakr and ‘Ali were left. And he waited for Allah’s permission to follow."
msgstr "“Ni Yathrib,” aliwaambia maswahaba wake, nao wakaondoka kwa siri kwenda Madinah, kundi baada ya kundi. Mwishowe, kati ya wale walioweza kuondoka, ni yeye, Abu Bakr na ‘Ali pekee waliobaki. Akasubiri ruhusa ya Allah ili awafuate."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "So his friends moved to Yathrib, the town we call Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ waited for Allah’s permission to follow."
msgstr "Basi marafiki zake walihamia Yathrib, mji tunaouita Madinah. Mtume ﷺ alisubiri ruhusa ya Allah ili awafuate."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr asked again and again to go. “Do not hurry,” he was told. “Perhaps Allah will give you a companion.” So he waited, hoping it would be the Prophet ﷺ, and fed two camels for four months to have them ready."
msgstr "Abu Bakr aliomba tena na tena aondoke. Akaambiwa, “Usiharakishe. Huenda Allah akakupa mwandamani.” Basi alisubiri, akitumaini kuwa mwandamani huyo angekuwa Mtume ﷺ. Kwa miezi minne aliwalisha ngamia wawili ili wawe tayari."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr wanted to go too. He was told to wait: perhaps Allah would give him a companion."
msgstr "Abu Bakr alitaka kuondoka pia. Aliambiwa asubiri: huenda Allah angempa mwandamani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then one day, in the full heat of noon, the Prophet ﷺ came at an hour he never came, and said, “Allah has given me permission to leave.” “Companionship?” Abu Bakr asked. “Companionship.” And Abu Bakr wept for joy."
msgstr "Kisha siku moja, wakati wa joto kali la adhuhuri, Mtume ﷺ alikuja kwa wakati ambao hakuwa akija kwa kawaida, akasema, “Allah ameniruhusu kuondoka.” Abu Bakr akauliza, “Tutaandamana pamoja?” “Ndiyo, pamoja,” akajibu. Abu Bakr akalia kwa furaha."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One hot noon, the Prophet ﷺ came with the news: they could go together! Abu Bakr cried for joy."
msgstr "Adhuhuri moja yenye joto kali, Mtume ﷺ alikuja na habari njema: wangeweza kuondoka pamoja! Abu Bakr akalia kwa furaha."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hired a guide to bring the camels to the cave of Thawr after three nights. Abu Bakr’s daughter Asma had nothing to tie up their food, so she split her waistband in two, and became “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Walimwajiri mwongoza njia aje na ngamia pangoni Thawr baada ya usiku tatu. Binti ya Abu Bakr, Asma, hakuwa na kitu cha kufungia chakula chao, kwa hiyo alipasua ukanda wake wa kiunoni vipande viwili. Hivyo akawa “mwenye mikanda miwili ya kiunoni”."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma had nothing to tie up their food, so she split her waistband in two and used that."
msgstr "Asma hakuwa na kitu cha kufungia chakula chao, kwa hiyo alipasua ukanda wake wa kiunoni vipande viwili na kuutumia."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, Quraysh had watched his companions go, and feared he would follow. In Dar al-Nadwah their leaders took Abu Jahl’s plan: young men from every clan would strike him together, spreading his blood across them all."
msgstr "Huko Makkah, Quraysh walikuwa wamewaona maswahaba wake wakiondoka, wakaogopa kwamba naye angefuata. Katika Dar al-Nadwah, viongozi wao walikubali mpango wa Abu Jahl: vijana kutoka kila ukoo wangemshambulia kwa pamoja, ili damu yake iwe juu ya koo zote."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The leaders of Makkah were afraid of the Prophet ﷺ, and they made a plan to attack him."
msgstr "Viongozi wa Makkah walimwogopa Mtume ﷺ, wakapanga kumshambulia."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night the men gathered at his door, waiting for him to sleep. He told ‘Ali to lie in his bed, wrapped in his green cloak. “Sleep in it,” he said. “Nothing you dislike will reach you from them.”"
msgstr "Usiku huo wanaume walikusanyika mlangoni pake, wakisubiri alale. Alimwambia ‘Ali alale kitandani mwake, akiwa amejifunika joho lake la kijani. “Lala ndani yake,” akasema. “Hakuna jambo usilolipenda litakalokupata kutoka kwao.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. ‘Ali lay in the Prophet’s bed, wrapped in his green cloak."
msgstr "Usiku huo walisubiri nje ya mlango wake. ‘Ali alilala kitandani mwa Mtume, akiwa amejifunika joho lake la kijani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then he came out to them with a handful of dust, scattering it over their heads and reciting, “So We have covered them, and they do not see.” Allah took their sight from him, and he went on his way."
msgstr "Kisha akawatokea akiwa na konzi ya mchanga, akawanyunyizia juu ya vichwa vyao huku akisoma, “Basi tukawafunika, nao hawaoni.” Allah aliwazuia wasimwone, naye akaendelea na safari yake."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ walked right out past them, scattering dust, and Allah kept them from seeing him."
msgstr "Mtume ﷺ alipita katikati yao akinyunyiza mchanga, na Allah akawazuia wasimwone."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came to Abu Bakr, and the two slipped out by a small door at the back of the house, Abu Bakr carrying all his savings. They did not take the road north to Madinah, but turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "Alimwendea Abu Bakr, nao wakatoka kwa siri kupitia mlango mdogo nyuma ya nyumba, Abu Bakr akiwa amebeba akiba yake yote. Hawakufuata njia ya kaskazini kuelekea Madinah, bali waligeukia kusini, upande wa Yemen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He and his best friend, Abu Bakr, slipped away in the dark. They went south, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "Yeye na rafiki yake wa karibu, Abu Bakr, waliondoka kwa siri gizani. Wakaelekea kusini, upande ulio kinyume na Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "About five miles on, they reached Mount Thawr and a cave in its side. Abu Bakr went in first, feeling his way in the dark, ready to take any harm himself. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Baada ya kusafiri takriban maili tano, walifika Mlima Thawr na pango lililokuwa ubavuni mwake. Abu Bakr aliingia kwanza, akitafuta njia gizani, tayari kujihatarisha ili kumlinda mwenzake. Kwa usiku tatu, pangoni hapo pangekuwa maficho yao."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They reached a cave on Mount Thawr. Abu Bakr went in first to make sure it was safe."
msgstr "Walifika kwenye pango la Mlima Thawr. Abu Bakr aliingia kwanza kuhakikisha kuwa lilikuwa salama."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As darkness settled, Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought his milking sheep to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. At dawn he drove the flock along ‘Abdullah’s trail, and the sheep wiped out his footprints."
msgstr "Giza lilipoingia, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, mtu aliyeachwa huru na Abu Bakr, alileta kondoo wake wa kukamuliwa pangoni ili wawili hao wapate maziwa freshi. Kulipopambazuka, aliwaongoza kondoo kufuata njia ya ‘Abdullah, nao wakafuta nyayo zake."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Amir brought sheep every evening for milk. In the morning, the sheep walked over ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "‘Amir alileta kondoo kila jioni ili wapate maziwa. Asubuhi, kondoo walipita juu ya nyayo za ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Searchers stood right above the cave! Abu Bakr was afraid they would look down. The Prophet ﷺ calmed his friend."
msgstr "Watafutaji walisimama juu kabisa ya pango! Abu Bakr aliogopa kwamba wangetazama chini. Mtume ﷺ akamtuliza rafiki yake."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the guide came with the camels, as arranged, and now there were four of them, with ‘Amir riding behind Abu Bakr. The guide led them down below Makkah and out along the coast, “by the edge of the sea.”"
msgstr "Kisha kiongozi akaja na ngamia kama ilivyopangwa. Sasa walikuwa wanne, huku ‘Amir akiwa amepanda nyuma ya Abu Bakr. Kiongozi akawaongoza chini ya Makkah na kufuata ufuo, “kando ya bahari.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After three nights, their guide came with the camels, and they rode out along the coast by the sea."
msgstr "Baada ya usiku tatu, kiongozi wao alifika na ngamia, nao wakapanda na kusafiri kando ya bahari."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People on the road knew Abu Bakr, but not the man with him. “Who is this man in front of you?” they asked. “This man guides me on the way,” he answered. They thought he meant the road; he meant the way of good."
msgstr "Watu waliokuwa njiani walimjua Abu Bakr, lakini hawakumjua mtu aliyekuwa pamoja naye. “Huyu mtu aliye mbele yako ni nani?” wakauliza. “Huyu ndiye anayeniongoza njiani,” akajibu. Walidhani alimaanisha njia ya safari; yeye alimaanisha njia ya wema."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People asked Abu Bakr who was with him. “He guides me on the way,” he said: the way of good."
msgstr "Watu walimuuliza Abu Bakr aliyekuwa pamoja naye ni nani. “Ananiongoza njiani,” akasema, akimaanisha njia ya wema."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh had put a price on the two. A man told Suraqah ibn Malik he had seen dark figures by the coast. “I knew that it was them,” Suraqah said, but he told the man otherwise. He wanted the hundred camels for himself."
msgstr "Quraysh ilikuwa imetangaza zawadi kwa atakayewapata hao wawili. Mtu mmoja alimwambia Suraqah ibn Malik kwamba alikuwa ameona watu weusi kwa mbali karibu na ufuo. “Nilijua kuwa ni wao,” Suraqah alisema, lakini akamwambia mtu huyo jambo tofauti. Alitaka ngamia mia hao ajipatie mwenyewe."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the road by the sea, a rider called Suraqah raced after them on his horse, hoping for a big reward."
msgstr "Akiwa njiani kando ya bahari, mpanda farasi aitwaye Suraqah aliwafuata kwa kasi, akitarajia kupata zawadi kubwa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode hard until he could hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. The Prophet ﷺ did not look back; Abu Bakr kept looking back. Then his horse’s forelegs sank into the ground up to the knees, and Suraqah fell."
msgstr "Alikimbiza farasi wake kwa nguvu hadi akaweza kumsikia Mtume ﷺ akisoma. Mtume ﷺ hakutazama nyuma; Abu Bakr aliendelea kutazama nyuma. Kisha miguu ya mbele ya farasi wake ikazama ardhini hadi magotini, na Suraqah akaanguka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah called out for safety and offered them provisions. They asked only, “Keep our whereabouts hidden.” ‘Amir wrote him a letter of safety on leather, and Suraqah rode back, turning every pursuer home."
msgstr "Suraqah aliomba usalama na akawapa chakula cha safari. Waliomba jambo moja tu: “Usimwambie mtu tulipo.” ‘Amir akamwandikia barua ya usalama kwenye ngozi, naye Suraqah akarudi nyuma, akiwafanya wote waliokuwa wakiwafuatilia warudi nyumbani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah gave up the chase. They asked him only to keep their secret, and he sent the other riders home."
msgstr "Suraqah aliacha kuwafuatilia. Walimwomba tu afiche walipo, naye akawatuma wapanda farasi wengine warudi nyumbani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They rode on, but their food had run out in a year of drought. By the road stood the two tents of Umm Ma‘bad, a woman who gave water and food to those who passed. They asked to buy meat and dates, but she had none."
msgstr "Wakaendelea na safari, lakini chakula chao kilikuwa kimeisha katika mwaka wa ukame. Kando ya njia palikuwa na mahema mawili ya Umm Ma‘bad, mwanamke aliyewapa maji na chakula wasafiri waliopita. Wakaomba kununua nyama na tende, lakini hakuwa navyo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hungry and far from home, they stopped at the tent of Umm Ma‘bad. She had no food to give them."
msgstr "Wakiwa na njaa na mbali na nyumbani, walisimama kwenye hema la Umm Ma‘bad. Hakuwa na chakula cha kuwapa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the back of her tent stood a ewe too weak to follow the flock. The Prophet ﷺ passed his hand over her udder, spoke the name of Allah, and milked until froth rose over the vessel. Umm Ma‘bad drank first, he drank last."
msgstr "Nyuma ya hema lake kulikuwa na kondoo jike aliyekuwa dhaifu sana kuweza kufuata kundi. Mtume ﷺ akapitisha mkono wake juu ya kiwele chake, akalitaja jina la Allah, kisha akamkamua hadi maziwa yakafurika kwenye chombo. Umm Ma‘bad ndiye aliyekunywa kwanza, naye akanywa wa mwisho."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Her thin sheep had no milk. The Prophet ﷺ said Allah’s name and milked her, and everyone drank!"
msgstr "Kondoo wake aliyekonda hakuwa na maziwa. Mtume ﷺ akalitaja jina la Allah na kumkamua, na kila mtu akanywa!"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When her husband came home, she described their guest: a man of shining beauty, his words like beads slipping from a string. “By Allah,” said Abu Ma‘bad, “that is the man from Quraysh.”"
msgstr "Mume wake aliporudi nyumbani, alimweleza kuhusu mgeni wao: mwanamume mwenye uzuri wa kung’aa, maneno yake yakitiririka kama shanga zinazoteleza kutoka kwenye uzi. “Wallahi,” akasema Abu Ma‘bad, “huyo ndiye yule mtu wa Quraysh.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When her husband came home, she told him about their guest: a shining face, and words like beads on a string."
msgstr "Mume wake aliporudi nyumbani, alimweleza kuhusu mgeni wao: uso wenye kung’aa na maneno kama shanga kwenye uzi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each morning the Muslims of Madinah watched for him till the heat drove them in. Then a man on a fort saw the travellers in white, shimmering in the mirage: “Here is your good fortune, the one you have been waiting for!”"
msgstr "Kila asubuhi Waislamu wa Madinah walikuwa wakimngojea hadi joto lilipowalazimisha kuingia ndani. Kisha mtu aliyekuwa kwenye ngome akawaona wasafiri waliovalia mavazi meupe wakimetameta kwenye sarabi: “Huyu ndiye mwenye bahati njema mnayemsubiri!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Madinah, people waited every morning in the hot sun. At last a man shouted: he is here!"
msgstr "Huko Madinah, watu walisubiri kila asubuhi chini ya jua kali. Hatimaye mtu mmoja akapaza sauti: amefika!"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him at Quba, in the shade of a palm with Abu Bakr. Most had never seen him, and they greeted Abu Bakr. Then the sun fell on the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr held his cloak over him, and at that they knew him."
msgstr "Walimpata Quba, akiwa pamoja na Abu Bakr kwenye kivuli cha mtende. Wengi wao hawakuwa wamewahi kumwona, kwa hiyo wakamsalimu Abu Bakr. Kisha jua likamwangazia Mtume ﷺ, Abu Bakr akamfunika kwa joho lake, ndipo wakamtambua."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him resting in the shade of a palm tree at Quba, with Abu Bakr beside him."
msgstr "Walimpata akipumzika kwenye kivuli cha mtende huko Quba, Abu Bakr akiwa kando yake."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There ‘Ali caught up with him, after three days in Makkah returning what people had left in the Prophet’s ﷺ care. The Prophet ﷺ founded his mosque at Quba and prayed in it, and on a Friday he rode on towards Madinah."
msgstr "Huko, ‘Ali alikutana naye baada ya kukaa Makkah kwa siku tatu, akirudisha vitu ambavyo watu walikuwa wamemkabidhi Mtume ﷺ avitunze. Mtume ﷺ alijenga msikiti wake Quba na kuswali humo. Siku ya Ijumaa akapanda ngamia kuelekea Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At Quba he built a mosque and prayed in it. Then he rode on into Madinah."
msgstr "Huko Quba alijenga msikiti na kuswali humo. Kisha akapanda ngamia na kuendelea hadi Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the way he prayed his first Friday prayer in Madinah. Clan after clan came out: “Stay with us. We have the numbers and the strength.” Each time he said of his camel, “Let her go her way; she is under orders.”"
msgstr "Njiani aliswali swala yake ya kwanza ya Ijumaa huko Madinah. Ukoo baada ya ukoo ulitoka kumkaribisha: “Kaa nasi. Tuna watu wengi na nguvu.” Kila mara alisema kuhusu ngamia wake: “Mwache aendelee na njia yake; ameelekezwa.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last the Prophet ﷺ rode into Madinah. Family after family asked him to stay, but he let his camel walk on."
msgstr "Hatimaye Mtume ﷺ aliingia Madinah akiwa amepanda ngamia. Familia baada ya familia zilimwomba akae kwao, lakini alimwacha ngamia wake aendelee."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The whole town poured out, and women on the rooftops strained to see: “Which one is he?” At last the camel knelt in a yard where dates were laid to dry. “This, if Allah wills, is the stopping place,” he said."
msgstr "Watu wote wa mji walimiminika nje, na wanawake waliokuwa juu ya paa walijaribu kuona: “Yupi ndiye yeye?” Hatimaye ngamia alipiga magoti kwenye ua ambamo tende zilikuwa zimeanikwa zikauke. “Hapa, Allah akipenda, ndipo tutakaposhukia,” akasema."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Children ran and people climbed up high to see him. His camel knelt in a yard where dates were dried."
msgstr "Watoto walikimbia, na watu wakapanda sehemu za juu ili wamwone. Ngamia wake alipiga magoti kwenye ua ambamo tende zilikaushwa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There his mosque rose, from bricks of sun-dried clay. The Prophet ﷺ carried them with the others, chanting, “O Allah, there is no good but the good of the Hereafter, so help the Ansar and the Emigrants.”"
msgstr "Huko msikiti wake ulijengwa kwa matofali ya udongo yaliyokaushwa juani. Mtume ﷺ aliyabeba pamoja na wengine huku akiimba, “Ewe Allah, hakuna kheri isipokuwa kheri ya Akhera, basi wape msaada Ansari na Muhajirina.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There they built a mosque, and the Prophet ﷺ carried bricks to help."
msgstr "Huko walijenga msikiti, na Mtume ﷺ alibeba matofali kuwasaidia."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the fever of Madinah laid his companions low. Makkah had been the dearest of lands to him, and now he prayed for their new home: “O Allah, make Madinah dear to us as You made Makkah dear to us, or dearer.”"
msgstr "Kisha homa ya Madinah ikawadhoofisha maswahaba wake. Makkah lilikuwa ndilo eneo alilolipenda zaidi, na sasa akaiombea makao yao mapya: “Ewe Allah, lifanye Madinah lipendeke kwetu kama ulivyolifanya Makkah lipendeke kwetu, au zaidi.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He prayed that Allah would make Madinah as dear to them as Makkah, and even dearer."
msgstr "Alimuomba Allah alifanye Madinah lipendeke kwao kama Makkah, na hata zaidi."

