msgid "Al-Bayhaqi, Dala'il al-Nubuwwah, 2/518"
msgstr "Al-Bayhaqi, Dala'il al-Nubuwwah, 2/518"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers came close, so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Watafutaji walikaribia sana, kiasi kwamba Abu Bakr alinong’ona, “Mmoja wao akitazama chini miguuni pake, atatuona.” Mtume ﷺ akajibu, “Unaonaje kuhusu watu wawili, ambaye wa tatu wao ni Allah?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Nor were they alone. Each night Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah came after dark with whatever Quraysh were plotting, then slipped back before dawn, so that morning found him in Makkah as if he had never left."
msgstr "Wala hawakuwa peke yao. Kila usiku, mwana wa Abu Bakr, ‘Abdullah, alikuja baada ya giza kuingia akiwa na habari za mipango ya Quraysh, kisha alirejea kisiri kabla ya alfajiri, ili alfajiri imkute Makkah kana kwamba hakuwa ameondoka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A home had to be offered before anyone could leave: the pledges at al-‘Aqabah gave the believers somewhere to go."
msgstr "Ili mtu aweze kuondoka, ilibidi kwanza awe na mahali pa kwenda: viapo vya uaminifu vya al-‘Aqabah viliwapa waumini mahali pa kwenda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Waiting on Allah’s permission and preparing every detail went together: camels fed for months, a guide hired, food packed."
msgstr "Kusubiri ruhusa ya Allah kulienda pamoja na kujiandaa kwa kila jambo: ngamia walilishwa kwa miezi, mwongoza njia akaajiriwa, na chakula kikaandaliwa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "His honesty held even then: on the night Quraysh plotted his death, he left ‘Ali to return all that Makkah had entrusted to him."
msgstr "Uaminifu wake ulidumu hata wakati huo: usiku ambao Quraysh walipanga kumuua, alimwacha ‘Ali arudishe kila kitu ambacho watu wa Makkah walikuwa wamemkabidhi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the most frightening moment came the calmest words: “Do not grieve; Allah is with us.”"
msgstr "Katika wakati wa kutisha zaidi, akasema maneno ya utulivu zaidi: “Usihuzunike; Allah yu pamoja nasi.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hunted as they were, they kept to the truth: “This man guides me on the way,” Abu Bakr said, and meant the way of good."
msgstr "Ingawa walikuwa wakiwindwa, waliendelea kusema ukweli: “Mtu huyu ananiongoza njiani,” Abu Bakr alisema, akimaanisha njia ya wema."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hearts can turn in a moment: the man who rode out to capture them rode back to send every pursuer home."
msgstr "Mioyo inaweza kubadilika kwa muda mfupi: mtu aliyeondoka kwa farasi kuwakamata alirudi akiwaamuru waliowafuatilia warudi nyumbani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Blessing came to a tent with nothing to give, and the Prophet ﷺ, who brought it, drank last of all."
msgstr "Baraka zilifika katika hema ambalo halikuwa na cha kutoa, na Mtume ﷺ, aliyezileta, ndiye aliyekunywa mwisho."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At Quba the Prophet ﷺ founded the first mosque where he prayed openly with his companions, a mosque built on God-consciousness."
msgstr "Huko Quba, Mtume ﷺ alianzisha msikiti wa kwanza ambamo aliswali waziwazi pamoja na maswahaba wake; msikiti uliojengwa juu ya uchamungu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Madinah became home by being built together: emigrants and Ansar raised the mosque side by side, and were made brothers."
msgstr "Madinah ikawa makazi kwa kujengwa pamoja: wahamiaji na Ansar walijenga msikiti bega kwa bega, kisha wakafanywa ndugu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "You followed the Hijrah from a promise made by night at al-‘Aqabah to a prayer for Madinah: a long wait, three nights in a cave, a hunter turned protector, and a whole town out to welcome him."
msgstr "Umefuatilia Hijrah kuanzia ahadi iliyotolewa usiku huko al-‘Aqabah hadi sala ya Madinah: kusubiri kwa muda mrefu, usiku tatu pangoni, mwindaji aliyekuwa mlinzi, na mji mzima uliotoka kumkaribisha."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "His home, where he waited for permission and from where he slipped out by night with Abu Bakr."
msgstr "Nyumbani kwake, ambako alisubiri ruhusa na alikotoka kisiri usiku pamoja na Abu Bakr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Where the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr hid in a cave for three nights while Quraysh searched for them."
msgstr "Mahali ambapo Mtume ﷺ na Abu Bakr walijificha pangoni kwa usiku tatu huku Quraysh wakiwatafuta."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The guide led them down to the sea and along the shore, station after station, towards Madinah."
msgstr "Mwongoza njia aliwaongoza kuelekea baharini na kando ya ufuo, wakipita kituo baada ya kituo kuelekea Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Where Madinah’s Muslims first met him, under a palm, and where he founded his mosque."
msgstr "Mahali ambapo Waislamu wa Madinah walikutana naye kwa mara ya kwanza chini ya mtende, na alipoanzisha msikiti wake."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Where his camel knelt, his mosque rose, and the emigrants made a new home."
msgstr "Mahali ambapo ngamia wake alipiga magoti, msikiti wake ukajengwa, na wahamiaji wakapata makazi mapya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Under Abu Ayyub’s roof"
msgstr "Chini ya paa la Abu Ayyub"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Ayyub carried the Prophet’s ﷺ saddle into his house. One day a jar of water broke upstairs, and he and his wife soaked it up with their only blanket, so that not a drop would fall on their guest."
msgstr "Abu Ayyub alibeba tandiko la Mtume ﷺ na kuliingiza nyumbani kwake. Siku moja mtungi wa maji ulivunjika ghorofani, naye na mkewe wakayafyonza maji kwa blanketi lao pekee, ili hata tone moja lisimdondokee mgeni wao."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When water spilled upstairs, Abu Ayyub and his wife mopped it up with their only blanket, so none dripped on him."
msgstr "Maji yalipomwagika ghorofani, Abu Ayyub na mkewe waliyafuta kwa blanketi lao pekee ili yasimdondokee."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "She of the two waistbands"
msgstr "Mwenye mikanda miwili ya kiunoni"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In another telling, it was at the cave that Asma’s waistband served them. She had brought their food but forgotten a strap to hang it by, so she split her waistband in two and hung the bag with one half."
msgstr "Katika simulizi nyingine, mkanda wa kiunoni wa Asma uliwasaidia pangoni. Alikuwa amewaletea chakula lakini akasahau kamba ya kukitundikia, kwa hiyo akaugawa mkanda wake wa kiunoni mara mbili na kutumia nusu moja kutundika mfuko."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma had nothing to tie up their food bag, so she split her waistband in two and used one half."
msgstr "Asma hakuwa na kitu cha kufungia mfuko wao wa chakula, kwa hiyo akaugawa mkanda wake wa kiunoni mara mbili na kutumia nusu moja."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ made each emigrant a brother to one of the Ansar who had taken them in. Each pair stood by the other and shared what they had, and at first such brothers even inherited from one another."
msgstr "Mtume ﷺ alimfanya kila mhamiaji kuwa ndugu wa mmoja wa Ansar waliowapokea. Kila jozi ilisaidiana na kugawana walichokuwa nacho, na mwanzoni ndugu hao hata walirithiana."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He made each newcomer a brother to someone from Madinah, so they would help each other and share."
msgstr "Alimfanya kila mgeni kuwa ndugu wa mtu kutoka Madinah, ili wasaidiane na kugawana walichokuwa nacho."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Let her go her way"
msgstr "Mwache aendelee na njia yake"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Even his mother’s kin, Banu ‘Adi ibn al-Najjar, called out, “Come to your mother’s people.” “Let her go her way,” he said. “She is under orders.” She walked on, and knelt among Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."
msgstr "Hata jamaa wa upande wa mama yake, Banu ‘Adi ibn al-Najjar, walimwita: “Njoo kwa watu wa mama yako.” Akasema: “Mwache aendelee na njia yake. Ameelekezwa.” Aliendelea na safari, kisha akapiga magoti kati ya Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Everyone wanted the Prophet ﷺ to stay with them. “Let my camel go,” he said. “She knows where to stop.”"
msgstr "Kila mtu alitaka Mtume ﷺ akae kwake. “Achia ngamia wangu aende,” alisema. “Anajua mahali pa kusimama.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode out of Quba on a Friday. On the way, the time for prayer came among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, and he prayed it in their mosque in the valley of Ranuna: his first Friday prayer in Madinah."
msgstr "Aliondoka Quba akiwa amepanda ngamia siku ya Ijumaa. Njiani, wakati wa sala ulifika alipokuwa miongoni mwa Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, naye akasali katika msikiti wao kwenye bonde la Ranuna: sala yake ya kwanza ya Ijumaa Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On his way into Madinah, the Prophet ﷺ stopped to lead the Friday prayer for the very first time there."
msgstr "Akiwa njiani kuelekea Madinah, Mtume ﷺ alisimama ili kuongoza sala ya Ijumaa kwa mara ya kwanza kabisa huko."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Dressed in white"
msgstr "Wakiwa wamevaa meupe"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the road they met al-Zubayr, coming home from Syria with Muslim merchants, and he dressed the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr in white. It was in white, shimmering in the mirage, that they were first seen from Madinah."
msgstr "Njiani walikutana na al-Zubayr, aliyekuwa akirejea kutoka Syria pamoja na wafanyabiashara Waislamu. Akamvisha Mtume ﷺ na Abu Bakr mavazi meupe. Wakiwa wamevaa meupe, yakimetameta kwenye upepo wa jangwani, ndivyo walivyoonekana kwa mara ya kwanza kutoka Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the way, their friend al-Zubayr gave them white clothes to wear."
msgstr "Njiani, rafiki yao al-Zubayr aliwapa nguo nyeupe za kuvaa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As he came, the women and children of Madinah sang: “The full moon has risen over us, from the passes of al-Wada‘. Thanks are due from us, as long as anyone calls to Allah.”"
msgstr "Alipowasili, wanawake na watoto wa Madinah waliimba: “Mwezi mpevu umetuchomozea, kutoka njia za milimani za al-Wada‘. Tunatoa shukrani, maadamu kuna anayemwita Allah.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The women and children sang a song of welcome: “The full moon has risen over us!”"
msgstr "Wanawake na watoto waliimba wimbo wa kumkaribisha: “Mwezi mpevu umetuchomozea!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "South, not north"
msgstr "Kuelekea kusini, si kaskazini"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Madinah lay to the north, but that was not the road they took. Under cover of night they turned the opposite way, south on the road towards Yemen, and went about five miles to Mount Thawr."
msgstr "Madinah ilikuwa kaskazini, lakini hawakupitia njia hiyo. Usiku, walielekea upande mwingine, kusini kwenye njia ya kuelekea Yemen, na kusafiri takriban maili tano hadi Mlima Thawr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Madinah was to the north, but they went south first, to a mountain called Thawr."
msgstr "Madinah ilikuwa kaskazini, lakini kwanza walielekea kusini, kwenye mlima uitwao Thawr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The road by the sea"
msgstr "Njia ya kando ya bahari"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The guide led them down below Makkah and along the coast, out onto the road below ‘Usfan. Then he took them by lower Amaj, and back to the road past Qudayd, one station after another."
msgstr "Mwongozi aliwaelekeza chini ya Makkah, wakafuata pwani hadi kwenye njia iliyo chini ya ‘Usfan. Kisha akawapitia Amaj ya chini, na kuwarudisha kwenye njia iliyopita Qudayd, kituo kimoja baada ya kingine."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Their guide knew the desert well. He led them down to the sea and along the coast, from one place to the next."
msgstr "Mwongozi wao aliijua jangwa vizuri. Aliwaongoza kuelekea baharini na kufuata pwani, kutoka sehemu moja hadi nyingine."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In the full heat of noon, someone called to Abu Bakr: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at the door, his head covered, at an hour he never came. “Allah has given me permission to leave,” he said."
msgstr "Wakati wa joto kali la adhuhuri, mtu mmoja alimwita Abu Bakr: Mtume wa Allah ﷺ alikuwa mlangoni, kichwa kikiwa kimefunikwa, katika saa ambayo hakuwa akija. “Allah amenipa ruhusa ya kuondoka,” alisema."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One hot noon the Prophet ﷺ knocked at Abu Bakr’s door with big news: “Allah has given me permission to leave.”"
msgstr "Adhuhuri moja yenye joto kali, Mtume ﷺ alibisha hodi kwenye mlango wa Abu Bakr akiwa na habari kubwa: “Allah amenipa ruhusa ya kuondoka.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "All his money"
msgstr "Pesa zake zote"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When Abu Bakr slipped out with the Prophet ﷺ that night, by a small door at the back of his house, he carried all his money with him: five or six thousand dirhams."
msgstr "Abu Bakr alipoondoka kisiri usiku huo pamoja na Mtume ﷺ kupitia mlango mdogo wa nyuma ya nyumba yake, alichukua pesa zake zote: dirham elfu tano au sita."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money with him for the journey, thousands of silver coins."
msgstr "Abu Bakr alichukua pesa zake zote kwa ajili ya safari, maelfu ya sarafu za fedha."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the mountain the trail grew confused, so the searchers climbed it and passed by the cave. Seeing a spider’s web across its entrance, they said, “If anyone had gone in here, there would be no web over it.”"
msgstr "Mlimani, njia haikuonekana wazi, hivyo waliokuwa wakiwatafuta walipanda mlima na kupita karibu na pango. Walipoona utando wa buibui kwenye mlango wake, wakasema, “Kama kuna mtu aliyeingia humu, kusingekuwa na utando juu yake.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers saw a spider’s web across the cave’s opening. “No one went in there,” they said, and walked on."
msgstr "Waliokuwa wakiwatafuta waliona utando wa buibui kwenye mlango wa pango. “Hakuna aliyeingia humo,” wakasema, kisha wakaendelea na safari."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah gives three nights. Which nights of the week they were was worked out by later biographers."
msgstr "‘Aishah anataja usiku tatu. Waandishi wa wasifu wa baadaye walibaini ni siku zipi za juma zilizohusika."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Into Madinah, on a Friday"
msgstr "Kuingia Madinah, siku ya Ijumaa"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Friday, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 September 622"
msgstr "Ijumaa, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 Septemba 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq gives the Friday he left Quba; the day of the month was worked out by a modern biographer."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq anataja Ijumaa aliyoondoka Quba; siku ya mwezi ilibainishwa na mwandishi wa wasifu wa kisasa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The guide comes with the camels"
msgstr "Mwongoza njia anakuja na ngamia"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Night of 1 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 16 September 622"
msgstr "Usiku wa tarehe 1 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 16 Septemba 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came after the third night, as agreed. Later biographers date it to the night of Monday."
msgstr "Alikuja baada ya usiku wa tatu, kama walivyokubaliana. Wanahistoria wa baadaye wanaiweka tarehe hiyo kuwa usiku wa Jumatatu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He had stayed on in Makkah through Muharram and Safar. The exact night was worked out by a modern biographer."
msgstr "Aliendelea kukaa Makkah katika miezi ya Muharram na Safar. Mwanahistoria wa kisasa ndiye aliyokadiria usiku husika."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A Monday in Rabi‘ al-Awwal · September 622"
msgstr "Jumatatu moja katika Rabi‘ al-Awwal · Septemba 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The reports agree it was a Monday. Ibn Ishaq gives the twelfth of the month; others give other days."
msgstr "Riwaya zinakubaliana kwamba ilikuwa Jumatatu. Ibn Ishaq anataja tarehe kumi na mbili ya mwezi huo; wengine wanataja siku tofauti."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah on their trail"
msgstr "Suraqah awafuatilia"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A Tuesday, after the noon rest at Qudayd"
msgstr "Jumanne, baada ya mapumziko ya adhuhuri huko Qudayd"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Sa‘d gives this day; the other reports tell what happened in order, but name no day."
msgstr "Ibn Sa‘d anataja siku hii; riwaya nyingine zinasimulia yaliyotokea kwa mpangilio, lakini hazitaji siku."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "From four days to fourteen nights"
msgstr "Kuanzia siku nne hadi usiku kumi na nne"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq counts Monday to Thursday; ‘Urwah speaks of ten nights and more, and Anas of fourteen."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq anahesabu kuanzia Jumatatu hadi Alhamisi; ‘Urwah anataja usiku kumi na zaidi, na Anas anataja kumi na nne."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how many went ahead to Madinah, while Abu Bakr held himself back to travel with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "‘Aishah anasimulia jinsi watu kadhaa walivyotangulia kwenda Madinah, huku Abu Bakr akijizuia kwenda ili asafiri pamoja na Mtume ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah recalls the family making them ready in haste, and Asma tying the food bag with a piece of her waistband."
msgstr "‘Aishah anakumbuka jinsi familia ilivyowaandalia vitu vyao kwa haraka, na Asma akafunga mfuko wa chakula kwa kipande cha ukanda wake wa kiunoni."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how her brother ‘Abdullah spent the nights with them, was among Quraysh by morning, and brought their news after dark."
msgstr "‘Aishah anasimulia jinsi ndugu yake ‘Abdullah alivyokaa nao usiku, akawa miongoni mwa Quraysh asubuhi, kisha akawaletea habari zao baada ya giza kuingia."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought his milking sheep to the cave after nightfall, on each of the three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah anasimulia jinsi ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah alivyoleta kondoo wake wa kukamuliwa pangoni baada ya giza kuingia, katika kila mmoja wa usiku huo mitatu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how they hired a skilled guide of Banu al-Dil, gave him their two camels, and set the meeting at Thawr."
msgstr "‘Aishah anasimulia jinsi walivyomwajiri mwongoza njia stadi kutoka Banu al-Dil, wakampa ngamia wao wawili, na kupanga kukutana Thawr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah and the guide set out with them, and how the guide took them by the coast road."
msgstr "‘Aishah anasimulia jinsi ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah na mwongoza njia walivyoondoka pamoja nao, na jinsi mwongoza njia alivyowapitisha kwenye njia ya pwani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how Madinah heard he had left Makkah, and how he stayed among Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf for ten nights and more."
msgstr "‘Urwah anasimulia jinsi habari za kuondoka kwake Makkah zilivyofika Madinah, na jinsi alivyokaa miongoni mwa Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf kwa usiku kumi na zaidi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how the yard was built into a mosque, with the Prophet ﷺ carrying bricks alongside the builders."
msgstr "‘Urwah anasimulia jinsi ua ulivyojengwa na kuwa msikiti, huku Mtume ﷺ akibeba matofali pamoja na wajenzi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah recalls the blood-money offered for each of the two, and a man who had just seen dark figures by the coast."
msgstr "Suraqah anakumbuka tuzo ya damu iliyotolewa kwa kila mmoja wa watu hao wawili, na mtu aliyekuwa amewaona watu kama vivuli vyeusi karibu na pwani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah describes hearing the Prophet ﷺ recite, Abu Bakr looking back, and his own horse sinking to its knees."
msgstr "Suraqah anaeleza jinsi alivyosikia Mtume ﷺ akisoma, Abu Bakr akigeuka kutazama nyuma, na farasi wake mwenyewe akizama hadi magotini."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah recalls that they took nothing he offered and asked only for secrecy, and that ‘Amir wrote him a letter of safety on leather."
msgstr "Suraqah anakumbuka kwamba hawakuchukua chochote alichowapa na waliomba tu afiche jambo hilo, na kwamba ‘Amir alimwandikia barua ya usalama kwenye ngozi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how he stayed among Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf, founded the mosque built on God-consciousness, and prayed in it."
msgstr "‘Urwah anasimulia jinsi alivyokaa miongoni mwa Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf, akajenga msikiti uliojengwa juu ya uchamungu, na kuswali humo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how people walked beside his camel until she knelt where his mosque now stands, then a yard for drying dates."
msgstr "‘Urwah anasimulia jinsi watu walivyotembea kando ya ngamia wake hadi akapiga magoti mahali ambapo msikiti wake unasimama sasa; wakati huo palikuwa ua wa kukaushia tende."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how Quraysh, now afraid of him, met in Dar al-Nadwah, the house where they settled all their affairs."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq anasimulia jinsi Quraysh, wakiwa sasa wanamwogopa, walivyokutana Dar al-Nadwah, nyumba ambamo walijadili na kuamua mambo yao yote."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Seeing the men at his door, the Prophet ﷺ tells ‘Ali to sleep in his bed under his green cloak, and promises him safety."
msgstr "Alipowaona wanaume mlangoni pake, Mtume ﷺ anamwambia ‘Ali alale kitandani mwake chini ya joho lake la kijani, na anamhakikishia usalama."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells why ‘Ali stayed behind: anyone in Makkah who feared for something precious had left it with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq anaeleza kwa nini ‘Ali alibaki nyuma: yeyote huko Makkah aliyehofia kitu cha thamani alikuwa amemwachia Mtume ﷺ akihifadhi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Ibn Ishaq’s telling she has no food and only dry ewes; he milks one until the bowl froths: “Drink, Umm Ma‘bad.”"
msgstr "Katika simulizi la Ibn Ishaq, hana chakula na ana kondoo-jike waliokauka tu; anamkamua mmoja hadi povu litokee kwenye bakuli: “Kunywa, Umm Ma‘bad.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah remembers the noon visit, and Abu Bakr asking at once to go with him: “Companionship?” “Yes.”"
msgstr "‘Aishah anakumbuka ziara ya adhuhuri, na Abu Bakr akiomba mara moja kwenda pamoja naye: “Nisafiri pamoja nawe?” “Ndiyo.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma recalls her father taking all his money, and the stones she laid where it had been kept, under a cloth, to calm her grandfather."
msgstr "Asma anakumbuka baba yake alipochukua pesa zake zote, na jinsi alivyoweka mawe mahali zilipokuwa zimehifadhiwa, chini ya kitambaa, ili kumtuliza babu yake."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri notes that he took the very opposite road from the one expected, south of Makkah towards Yemen."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri anabainisha kwamba alichukua njia iliyo kinyume kabisa na ile iliyotarajiwa, kuelekea kusini mwa Makkah, upande wa Yemen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq places Asma’s waistband at the cave, and gives it as the reason she was called Dhat al-Nitaqayn."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq anasema Asma alitumia mkanda wake pangoni, na anaeleza kwamba ndiyo sababu aliitwa Dhat al-Nitaqayn."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn ‘Abbas tells of the web across the cave’s mouth; Ibn Kathir counts this among the best reports of it."
msgstr "Ibn ‘Abbas anasimulia kuhusu utando wa buibui kwenye mdomo wa pango; Ibn Kathir anauhesabu miongoni mwa masimulizi bora zaidi kuhusu jambo hilo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq names the places on the guide’s route, one by one, from below Makkah to the road beyond Qudayd."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq anataja maeneo yaliyokuwa kwenye njia ya mwongoza msafara, moja baada ya jingine, kutoka kusini mwa Makkah hadi barabara iliyopita Qudayd."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells of the meeting with al-Zubayr’s caravan of Muslim merchants, and the white clothes he gave the two travellers."
msgstr "‘Urwah anasimulia kuhusu kukutana na msafara wa wafanyabiashara Waislamu wa al-Zubayr, na mavazi meupe aliyowapa wasafiri hao wawili."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri tells of the first Friday prayer among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, with a hundred men, in the mosque in the valley."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri anasimulia kuhusu swala ya kwanza ya Ijumaa miongoni mwa Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, iliyoswaliwa na wanaume mia moja katika msikiti wa bondeni."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how each clan was answered, “Let her go, for she is under orders,” until she knelt among Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq anasimulia jinsi kila ukoo ulivyojibiwa, “Mwache aende, kwa maana ameagizwa,” hadi akapiga magoti miongoni mwa Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how he lodged with Abu Ayyub until his mosque and rooms were built, working on them with emigrants and Ansar."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq anasimulia jinsi alivyokaa kwa Abu Ayyub hadi msikiti na vyumba vyake vilipojengwa, akifanya kazi hiyo pamoja na wahajiri na Ansar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir’s heading for the brotherhood: the Prophet ﷺ paired emigrants with Ansar so each newcomer had someone to lean on."
msgstr "Kichwa cha Ibn Kathir kuhusu udugu: Mtume ﷺ aliwaunganisha wahajiri na Ansar ili kila mgeni apate mtu wa kumtegemea."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn ‘A'ishah, a later narrator who does not say who told him, describes women and children singing as the Prophet ﷺ arrived."
msgstr "Ibn ‘A'ishah, mpokezi wa baadaye ambaye hasemi aliyemsimulia, anaeleza wanawake na watoto wakiimba Mtume ﷺ alipowasili."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri dates the night he left his house: 27 Safar, in the fourteenth year of his prophethood."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri anataja tarehe ya usiku alipoondoka nyumbani kwake: 27 Safar, katika mwaka wa kumi na nne wa utume wake."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri names the three nights in the cave: the nights before Friday, Saturday and Sunday."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri anataja usiku mitatu pangoni: usiku wa kuamkia Ijumaa, Jumamosi na Jumapili."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri dates the guide’s coming with the two camels to the night of Monday, the first of Rabi‘ al-Awwal."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri anaweka tarehe ya mwongoza msafara kufika na ngamia wawili kuwa usiku wa kuamkia Jumatatu, tarehe moja Rabi‘ al-Awwal."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah gives the day he came down among Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf: a Monday in the month of Rabi‘ al-Awwal."
msgstr "‘Urwah anataja siku aliyofika miongoni mwa Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf: Jumatatu katika mwezi wa Rabi‘ al-Awwal."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir sets Ibn Ishaq’s four days, Monday to Thursday, beside ‘Urwah’s report of ten nights and more."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir analinganisha siku nne za Ibn Ishaq, kuanzia Jumatatu hadi Alhamisi, na simulizi la ‘Urwah la usiku kumi na zaidi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri dates his arrival among Banu al-Najjar to Friday, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal, in the first year of the Hijrah."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri anaweka tarehe ya kuwasili kwake miongoni mwa Banu al-Najjar kuwa Ijumaa, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal, katika mwaka wa kwanza wa Hijrah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir gives her name, ‘Atikah, and her family, and calls her story well known, through routes that support one another."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir anataja jina lake, ‘Atikah, na familia yake, na anasema simulizi lake linajulikana sana, likisimuliwa kupitia njia zinazothibitishana."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Stones under a cloth"
msgstr "Mawe chini ya kitambaa"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money, five or six thousand dirhams. When his blind father came, fearing it gone, Asma laid stones in its niche under a cloth and let him feel them."
