#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. ‘Ali lay in the Prophet’s ﷺ bed, wrapped in his green cloak."
msgstr "Usiku huo walisubiri nje ya mlango wake. ‘Ali alilala kitandani mwa Mtume ﷺ, akiwa amejifunika kwa joho lake la kijani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s helper ‘Amir brought sheep each evening for milk. At dawn the sheep walked over ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "‘Amir, msaidizi wa Abu Bakr, alileta kondoo kila jioni ili wapate maziwa. Kulipopambazuka, kondoo walipita juu ya nyayo za ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Some say it was here that Abu Bakr’s daughter Asma split her waistband in two, to tie up their food bag."
msgstr "Wengine husema kuwa hapa ndipo Asma, binti ya Abu Bakr, alipogawanya ukanda wake wa kiunoni vipande viwili ili kufunga mfuko wao wa chakula."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money. To calm her blind grandfather, his daughter Asma let him feel stones under a cloth."
msgstr "Abu Bakr alichukua mali yake yote. Ili kumtuliza babu yake aliyekuwa kipofu, binti yake Asma alimruhusu aguse mawe yaliyokuwa chini ya kitambaa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Friday 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 September 622"
msgstr "Ijumaa 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 Septemba 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq has him stay at Quba Monday to Thursday and ride on the Friday; a modern biographer worked out the date."
msgstr "Kwa mujibu wa Ibn Ishaq, alikaa Quba kuanzia Jumatatu hadi Alhamisi, kisha akasafiri siku ya Ijumaa; mwandishi wa wasifu wa kisasa alihesabu tarehe hiyo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Bukhari’s report has him come on the morning of the third day; later biographers date it to the night of Monday."
msgstr "Riwaya ya Al-Bukhari inasema alifika asubuhi ya siku ya tatu; waandishi wa wasifu wa baadaye waliweka tarehe hiyo kuwa usiku wa Jumatatu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Monday 8 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 23 September 622"
msgstr "Jumatatu 8 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 23 Septemba 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The reports agree on a Monday. A modern biographer worked out the date; Ibn Ishaq gives the twelfth."
msgstr "Riwaya zinakubaliana kuwa ilikuwa Jumatatu. Mwandishi wa wasifu wa kisasa alihesabu tarehe hiyo; Ibn Ishaq anataja tarehe ya kumi na mbili."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After the noon rest at Qudayd"
msgstr "Baada ya kupumzika mchana huko Qudayd"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Sa‘d calls it a Tuesday, by his own count of the days; the other reports name no day."
msgstr "Ibn Sa‘d anasema ilikuwa Jumanne, kwa kufuata hesabu yake mwenyewe ya siku; riwaya nyingine hazitaji siku."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every pilgrimage season, as the tribes came to Makkah, the Prophet ﷺ went out to them and called them to Allah. One season, at a place called al-‘Aqabah, six men from Yathrib sat down to listen."
msgstr "Kila msimu wa hija, makabila yalipokuja Makkah, Mtume ﷺ aliwaendea na kuwaita wamwamini Allah. Msimu mmoja, katika sehemu iitwayo al-‘Aqabah, wanaume sita kutoka Yathrib waliketi kumsikiliza."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every year, pilgrims came to Makkah. The Prophet ﷺ told them about Allah, and six men from Yathrib listened."
msgstr "Kila mwaka, mahujaji walikuja Makkah. Mtume ﷺ aliwaeleza kuhusu Allah, na wanaume sita kutoka Yathrib wakamsikiliza."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At home their Jewish neighbours often warned of a prophet soon to come. “By Allah,” the six said to one another, “this is the prophet they threatened us with.” They accepted Islam and took it home."
msgstr "Kwao, majirani zao Wayahudi mara nyingi waliwaonya kwamba nabii angekuja hivi karibuni. “Wallahi,” wale sita waliambiana, “huyu ndiye nabii waliyotutisha kwa habari zake.” Waliukubali Uislamu na kurudi nao nyumbani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Their Jewish neighbours said a prophet was coming. “This is him!” the six men said, and they became Muslims."
msgstr "Majirani zao Wayahudi walisema kwamba nabii alikuwa anakuja. “Huyu ndiye!” wakasema wale wanaume sita, kisha wakawa Waislamu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, those who followed the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ were insulted and harmed by Quraysh, his own tribe, who ruled the town. This is the story of the Hijrah: how they found a new home, and how he made the journey there."
msgstr "Huko Makkah, watu waliomfuata Mtume Muhammad ﷺ walitukanwa na kudhuriwa na Quraysh, kabila lake mwenyewe lililotawala mji huo. Hii ndiyo hadithi ya Hijrah: jinsi walivyopata makao mapya na jinsi alivyofunga safari kwenda huko."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, the Prophet’s ﷺ own tribe was cruel to the Muslims. This is the story of how they found a new home."
msgstr "Huko Makkah, kabila la Mtume ﷺ mwenyewe liliwatendea Waislamu kwa ukatili. Hii ndiyo hadithi ya jinsi walivyopata makao mapya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every pilgrimage season, as tribes from across Arabia came to Makkah, the Prophet ﷺ went out to them and called them to Allah. One season, at al-‘Aqabah, six men from Yathrib, a town to the north, sat down to listen."
msgstr "Kila msimu wa hija, makabila kutoka sehemu mbalimbali za Arabia yalipokuja Makkah, Mtume ﷺ aliwaendea na kuwalingania kwa Allah. Msimu mmoja, huko al-‘Aqabah, wanaume sita kutoka Yathrib, mji ulioko kaskazini, waliketi kumsikiliza."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every year, visitors came to Makkah to worship. The Prophet ﷺ told them about Allah, and six men from Yathrib listened."
msgstr "Kila mwaka, wageni walikuja Makkah kuabudu. Mtume ﷺ aliwaeleza kuhusu Allah, na wanaume sita kutoka Yathrib wakamsikiliza."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Back home, their Jewish neighbours used to say a prophet would soon come, and they would follow him against them. “By Allah,” the six said to one another, “this is that prophet.” They accepted Islam and took it home."
msgstr "Waliporudi nyumbani, majirani wao Wayahudi walikuwa wakisema kwamba nabii angekuja hivi karibuni na kwamba wangemfuata ili kupigana nao. “Wallahi,” wale sita waliambiana, “huyu ndiye nabii huyo.” Wakasilimu na kupeleka Uislamu nyumbani kwao."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Back home, their Jewish neighbours said a prophet was coming. “This is him!” the six said, and they became Muslims."
msgstr "Waliporudi nyumbani, majirani wao Wayahudi walisema kwamba nabii alikuwa anakuja. “Huyu ndiye!” wale sita wakasema, nao wakawa Waislamu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each year more came from Yathrib, until seventy-three men and two women met him there by night. They pledged to protect him, if he came, as they protected their own families. “I am of you and you are of me,” he said."
msgstr "Kila mwaka, watu zaidi walikuja kutoka Yathrib, hadi wanaume sabini na watatu na wanawake wawili walipokutana naye huko usiku. Waliahidi kumlinda akija, kama walivyolinda familia zao wenyewe. “Mimi ni wenu, nanyi ni wangu,” akasema."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Later, many more came from Yathrib at night. They promised to keep him safe, the way they kept their own families safe."
msgstr "Baadaye, watu wengi zaidi kutoka Yathrib walikuja usiku. Waliahidi kumlinda, kama walivyolinda familia zao wenyewe."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Their new home, he told his companions, would be Yathrib, soon to be called Madinah. Group by group these Emigrants slipped away, until few were left but him, his close friend Abu Bakr and his cousin ‘Ali."
msgstr "Aliwaambia maswahaba wake kwamba makao yao mapya yangekuwa Yathrib, ambayo baadaye ingeitwa Madinah. Muhajirun hawa waliondoka kimyakimya, kundi baada ya kundi, hadi waliobaki walikuwa wachache tu: yeye, rafiki yake wa karibu Abu Bakr na binamu yake ‘Ali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "So the Muslims of Makkah moved to Yathrib, the town we call Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ waited for Allah’s permission to go."
msgstr "Hivyo Waislamu wa Makkah walihamia Yathrib, mji tunaouita Madinah. Mtume ﷺ alingoja ruhusa ya Allah ili aondoke."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr asked again and again to go too. “Do not hurry,” the Prophet ﷺ told him. “Perhaps Allah will give you a companion.” Abu Bakr hoped it would be the Prophet ﷺ himself, and fed two camels for four months."
msgstr "Abu Bakr aliomba tena na tena aondoke pia. “Usiharakishe,” Mtume ﷺ alimwambia. “Huenda Allah akakupa mwenzi wa safari.” Abu Bakr alitumaini kwamba mwenzi huyo angekuwa Mtume ﷺ mwenyewe, akawatunza ngamia wawili kwa miezi minne."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then one noon, at an hour he never came, the Prophet ﷺ came to Abu Bakr’s house. “Allah has given me permission to leave.” “And I am to come with you?” Abu Bakr asked. “Yes.” And Abu Bakr wept for joy."
msgstr "Kisha siku moja adhuhuri, wakati ambao hakuwa akija kamwe, Mtume ﷺ alifika nyumbani kwa Abu Bakr. “Allah ameniruhusu kuondoka.” “Nami nitakwenda pamoja nawe?” Abu Bakr akauliza. “Ndiyo.” Abu Bakr akalia kwa furaha."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hired a guide to bring the camels after three nights to a cave on Mount Thawr, where they would hide. Asma, Abu Bakr’s daughter, split her waistband to tie up their food, and became “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Waliajiri mwongoza njia alete ngamia baada ya usiku tatu kwenye pango la Mlima Thawr, ambako wangejificha. Asma, binti ya Abu Bakr, alipasua ukanda wake wa kiunoni ili kufungia chakula chao, na akajulikana kama “mwenye mikanda miwili ya kiunoni”."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh feared the Prophet ﷺ would follow his companions. In their council house, their leaders agreed to kill him: a young man from every clan would strike at once, so that no one clan could be made to answer for it."
msgstr "Quraysh waliogopa kwamba Mtume ﷺ angewafuata maswahaba wake. Katika nyumba yao ya mashauriano, viongozi wao walikubaliana kumuua: kijana mmoja kutoka kila ukoo angemshambulia kwa wakati mmoja, ili ukoo mmoja pekee usiwajibishwe kwa hilo."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last Allah gave him permission. But the leaders of Makkah, afraid of his message, made a plan to hurt him."
msgstr "Hatimaye Allah alimpa ruhusa. Lakini viongozi wa Makkah, wakiogopa ujumbe wake, walipanga kumdhuru."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. His cousin ‘Ali lay in his bed, so they would think the Prophet ﷺ was inside."
msgstr "Usiku huo, walingoja nje ya mlango wake. Binamu yake ‘Ali alilala kitandani mwake, ili wafikiri kwamba Mtume ﷺ alikuwa ndani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then he came out to them with a handful of dust, scattering it over their heads and reciting the Quran: “So We have covered them, and they do not see.” Allah took their sight from him, and he went on his way."
msgstr "Kisha akawatokea akiwa na konzi ya udongo, akawamwagia juu ya vichwa vyao huku akisoma Quran: “Basi tumewafunika, hivyo hawaoni.” Allah aliwazuia wasimwone, naye akaendelea na safari yake."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ walked right out past them, throwing a handful of dust, and Allah kept them from seeing him."
msgstr "Mtume ﷺ alipita katikati yao moja kwa moja, akirusha konzi ya udongo, na Allah akawazuia wasimwone."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came to Abu Bakr, and the two slipped out by a small door at the back of Abu Bakr’s house, Abu Bakr carrying all his savings. Madinah lay to the north, but they turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "Alimwendea Abu Bakr, kisha wote wawili wakatoka kimyakimya kupitia mlango mdogo nyuma ya nyumba ya Abu Bakr, ambaye alibeba akiba yake yote. Madinah ilikuwa upande wa kaskazini, lakini walielekea kusini, upande wa Yemen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He and his best friend, Abu Bakr, slipped away in the dark. They went south first, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "Yeye na rafiki yake wa karibu Abu Bakr waliondoka kimyakimya gizani. Kwanza walielekea kusini, upande ulio kinyume na Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hid in a cave on Mount Thawr. Abu Bakr went in first to make sure it was safe."
msgstr "Walijificha katika pango la Mlima Thawr. Abu Bakr aliingia kwanza kuhakikisha kwamba pango lilikuwa salama."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh sent out searchers, and they came so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” “What do you think of two,” said the Prophet ﷺ, “when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Quraysh walituma watu kuwatafuta, nao wakaja karibu sana kiasi kwamba Abu Bakr akanong’ona, “Kama mmoja wao angeangalia chini miguuni pake, angetuona.” “Unaonaje kuhusu wawili,” Mtume ﷺ akasema, “ambaye Allah ni wa tatu wao?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Men from Makkah searched everywhere, and stood right above the cave! Abu Bakr was afraid. The Prophet ﷺ calmed him."
msgstr "Wanaume kutoka Makkah walitafuta kila mahali, wakasimama juu kabisa ya pango! Abu Bakr aliogopa. Mtume ﷺ akamtuliza."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As darkness settled, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, who tended Abu Bakr’s sheep, brought the flock to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. At dawn he drove it along ‘Abdullah’s trail, and the sheep wiped out ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "Giza lilipoingia, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, aliyekuwa akichunga kondoo wa Abu Bakr, alileta kundi hilo pangoni ili wale wawili wapate maziwa freshi. Kulipopambazuka, aliwaendesha kondoo wakifuata njia ya ‘Abdullah, nao wakafuta nyayo za ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s helper ‘Amir brought sheep each evening for milk. At dawn the sheep covered up ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "Msaidizi wa Abu Bakr, ‘Amir, alileta kondoo kila jioni ili wapate maziwa. Kulipopambazuka, kondoo walifunika nyayo za ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh offered a hundred camels for the two. Suraqah ibn Malik, a horseman of a tribe on the coast road, heard that riders had been seen by the sea. He knew it was them, but kept quiet: he wanted the reward himself."
msgstr "Quraysh walitoa ngamia mia moja kwa ajili ya watu hao wawili. Suraqah ibn Malik, mpanda farasi kutoka kabila lililoishi kando ya njia ya pwani, alisikia kwamba wapanda farasi walikuwa wameonekana karibu na bahari. Alijua kuwa hao walikuwa wao, lakini akakaa kimya: alitaka zawadi hiyo ajipatie mwenyewe."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After three nights they rode on by the sea. A rider called Suraqah raced after them, hoping for a reward."
msgstr "Baada ya usiku tatu, waliendelea na safari kwa farasi kando ya bahari. Mpanda farasi mmoja aliyeitwa Suraqah akawafuatia kwa kasi, akitarajia kupata zawadi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode hard until he could hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. The Prophet ﷺ did not look back; Abu Bakr kept looking back. Then Suraqah’s horse sank into the ground up to its knees, and he fell."
msgstr "Alikimbiza farasi wake kwa kasi hadi akaweza kumsikia Mtume ﷺ akisoma. Mtume ﷺ hakutazama nyuma; Abu Bakr aliendelea kutazama nyuma. Kisha farasi wa Suraqah akazama ardhini hadi magotini, naye akaanguka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Shaken, Suraqah begged them for a promise of safety and offered them provisions. They asked only, “Keep our whereabouts hidden.” ‘Amir wrote the promise on leather, and Suraqah rode back, turning every pursuer home."
msgstr "Akiwa ameshtuka, Suraqah aliwaomba wamhakikishie usalama wake na akawapa chakula cha safari. Waliomba jambo moja tu: “Ficha tulipo.” ‘Amir aliandika ahadi hiyo kwenye ngozi, naye Suraqah akarudi kwa farasi, akiwageuza wote waliokuwa wakiwafuatilia warudi nyumbani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah gave up the chase. They asked him to tell no one where they were, and he sent other searchers the wrong way."
msgstr "Suraqah aliacha kuwafuatilia. Walimwomba asimwambie mtu yeyote walipokuwa, naye akawapeleka watafutaji wengine njia isiyo sahihi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hungry and far from home, they stopped at the tent of a woman called Umm Ma‘bad. She had no food to give them."
msgstr "Wakiwa na njaa na mbali na nyumbani, walisimama kwenye hema la mwanamke aliyeitwa Umm Ma‘bad. Hakuwa na chakula cha kuwapa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Her thin sheep had no milk. The Prophet ﷺ said Allah’s name and milked the sheep, and everyone drank!"
msgstr "Kondoo wake aliyekuwa amekonda hakuwa na maziwa. Mtume ﷺ alilitaja jina la Allah na kumkamua kondoo, nao wote wakanywa!"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After they left, her husband came home. She told him of their guest: a shining face, and words like beads on a string."
msgstr "Baada ya kuondoka, mume wake alirudi nyumbani. Akamweleza kuhusu mgeni wao: uso uliomeremeta na maneno kama shanga zilizopangwa kwenye uzi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each morning the Ansar, the Muslims of Madinah, watched for him until the heat drove them in. Then a man on a fort saw the travellers in white, shimmering in the mirage: “Here is the one you have been waiting for!”"
msgstr "Kila asubuhi Ansar, Waislamu wa Madinah, walimsubiri hadi joto lilipowalazimisha kurudi ndani. Kisha mtu aliyekuwa kwenye ngome akawaona wasafiri waliovalia mavazi meupe, wakimetameta kwenye kiangazi cha upepo: “Yuko hapa yule mliyemsubiri!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him at Quba, a village just outside Madinah, resting under a palm with Abu Bakr. Most had never seen him, and greeted Abu Bakr, until the sun fell on the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr shaded him with his cloak."
msgstr "Walimkuta Quba, kijiji kilicho nje kidogo ya Madinah, akiwa amepumzika chini ya mtende pamoja na Abu Bakr. Wengi hawakuwa wamewahi kumwona, hivyo wakamsalimu Abu Bakr, hadi jua lilipomwangazia Mtume ﷺ na Abu Bakr akamkinga kwa joho lake."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Ali caught up with him there. He had stayed three days in Makkah to return what people had left in the Prophet’s ﷺ care. At Quba the Prophet ﷺ founded his mosque, and on a Friday he rode on towards Madinah."
msgstr "‘Ali alimfikia huko. Alikuwa amebaki Makkah kwa siku tatu ili kurudisha vitu ambavyo watu walikuwa wameweka chini ya uangalizi wa Mtume ﷺ. Huko Quba, Mtume ﷺ alianzisha msikiti wake, na siku ya Ijumaa akaendelea kwa farasi kuelekea Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last the Prophet ﷺ rode into Madinah on his camel. Everyone asked him to stay, but he let the camel choose the way."
msgstr "Hatimaye Mtume ﷺ aliingia Madinah akiwa amepanda ngamia wake. Kila mtu alimwomba akae kwake, lakini akamwacha ngamia achague njia."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People climbed up high to see him. His camel knelt in a yard where dates were dried, and there he made his home."
msgstr "Watu walipanda sehemu za juu ili wamuone. Ngamia wake alipiga magoti kwenye ua ambamo tende zilikaushwa, na hapo ndipo alipofanya makazi yake."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He prayed that Allah would make the Muslims love Madinah as much as Makkah, and even more."
msgstr "Aliomba Allah awafanye Waislamu waipende Madinah kama wanavyoipenda Makkah, na hata zaidi."

