msgstr "Hatua inayofuata"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Closer and closer he came, until he could hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. The Prophet ﷺ never looked back; Abu Bakr kept turning round. As Suraqah drew near, the ground gave way: his horse sank to its knees, and he fell."
msgstr "Alizidi kusogea, mpaka akaweza kumsikia Mtume ﷺ akisoma. Mtume ﷺ hakutazama nyuma kamwe; Abu Bakr aliendelea kugeuka kutazama nyuma. Suraqah alipokaribia, ardhi ililegea: farasi wake alizama mpaka magotini, naye akaanguka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the cry the Muslims hurried out to meet him, and he went with them to Quba, just outside Madinah. Most had never seen him and greeted Abu Bakr, until the sun fell on the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr shaded him with his cloak."
msgstr "Waliposikia mwito huo, Waislamu waliharakisha kutoka kwenda kumlaki, naye akaenda pamoja nao hadi Quba, nje kidogo ya Madinah. Wengi wao walikuwa hawajawahi kumwona, hivyo wakamsalimu Abu Bakr, mpaka jua lilipomwangazia Mtume ﷺ na Abu Bakr akamkinga kwa joho lake."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Word had reached Madinah that the Prophet ﷺ had left Makkah. Every morning after the dawn prayer, its Muslims, the Ansar, walked out to the edge of the lava plain and watched for him, until the sun took the last of the shade and drove them home."
msgstr "Habari zilikuwa zimefika Madinah kwamba Mtume ﷺ alikuwa ameondoka Makkah. Kila asubuhi baada ya sala ya alfajiri, Waislamu wake, Ansar, walitembea hadi ukingo wa uwanda wa lava na kumtazama, mpaka jua lilipoondoa kivuli cha mwisho na kuwarudisha nyumbani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Madinah, people went out every morning to wait for him, until the sun grew too hot."
msgstr "Huko Madinah, watu walitoka kila asubuhi kumsubiri, mpaka jua lilipokuwa kali sana."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One day, when they had already given up and gone in, the first to see him was not one of them at all. A Jewish man on one of the forts saw the travellers in white, shimmering in the mirage: “Here is the one you have been waiting for!”"
msgstr "Siku moja, walipokuwa tayari wamekata tamaa na kurudi ndani, mtu wa kwanza kumwona hakuwa mmoja wao hata kidogo. Mwanamume Myahudi akiwa juu ya mojawapo ya ngome aliona wasafiri waliovaa mavazi meupe wakimetameta kwenye mawimbi ya hewa ya joto: “Yule mliyemsubiri yuko hapa!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One day, a man up on a tower saw travellers in white coming. “He is here!” he shouted."
msgstr "Siku moja, mwanamume aliyekuwa juu ya mnara aliwaona wasafiri waliovaa mavazi meupe wakija. “Yuko hapa!” akapiga kelele."

#: src/lib/scene-manifest.js
msgid "N05c"
msgstr "N05c"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Those first months were hard: Madinah was then a land of fever. Abu Bakr and Bilal fell ill, and Bilal longed aloud for the valleys of Makkah. So the Prophet ﷺ prayed: “O Allah, make Madinah dear to us as You made Makkah dear to us, or dearer.”"
msgstr "Miezi ile ya kwanza ilikuwa migumu: wakati huo Madinah ilikuwa mahali penye homa nyingi. Abu Bakr na Bilal waliugua, na Bilal alitamani kwa sauti mabonde ya Makkah. Basi Mtume ﷺ akaomba: “Ewe Allah, tufanye tuipende Madinah kama tulivyoipenda Makkah, au zaidi.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr offered him one of the two camels he had kept ready. “At its price,” the Prophet ﷺ said. They handed both to a guide they had hired, to bring to Mount Thawr after three nights."
msgstr "Abu Bakr alimtolea ngamia mmoja kati ya wawili aliokuwa amewaweka tayari. “Kwa bei yake,” akasema Mtume ﷺ. Wakawakabidhi wote wawili kwa mwongoza njia waliyekuwa wamemwajiri, awapeleke kwenye Mlima Thawr baada ya usiku tatu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr gave a guide their two camels, to bring to a mountain called Thawr after three nights."
msgstr "Abu Bakr alimkabidhi mwongoza njia ngamia wao wawili, awapeleke kwenye mlima unaoitwa Thawr baada ya usiku tatu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then food was made ready for the road. There was nothing to tie the bag with, so Asma, Abu Bakr’s daughter, split her waistband in two, and from then on she was called “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Kisha chakula kikaandaliwa kwa ajili ya safari. Hawakuwa na kitu cha kufungia mfuko, hivyo Asma, binti ya Abu Bakr, akapasua ukanda wake wa kiunoni vipande viwili. Tangu hapo akajulikana kama “mwenye mikanda miwili ya kiunoni”."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Abu Bakr’s house, Asma made their food for the road. Finding nothing to tie the bag and the water skin with, she told her father, “Only my waistband.” “Split it in two,” he said, and so she was called “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Katika nyumba ya Abu Bakr, Asma aliwaandalia chakula cha safari. Alipokosa kitu cha kufungia mfuko na kiriba cha maji, alimwambia baba yake, “Nina ukanda wangu tu.” “Ukatayie sehemu mbili,” akasema, ndipo akaitwa “mwenye mikanda miwili”."
